# =====================================================================================
# dual_grounding.ttl — the REUSED SP1 dual-grounding of the crs coordinate-chart classes (W2 · SP3, Task T11).
# =====================================================================================
# Plan Task T11 ("Every new crs: carrier/tower/geometer/plane/product owl:Class carries its own
# prim:Realization (aob:groundingClaim-style) + reflexive carrier + prim:Primitive so SP1's
# prim:DualGroundingShape / q_universality stays green on the merged graph. Tooth:
# q_chart_dual_grounded (reuses SP1). Probe: strip one crs class's realization -> SP1 q_universality
# flips false.") and design §3/§4 ("SP3 adds owl:Classes that fall under SP1's prim:DualGroundingShape /
# q_universality ... every new carrier/tower/geometer class carries its own prim:Realization + reflexive
# carrier + prim:Primitive"; "Reused SP1 tooth: each new carrier/tower/geometer owl:Class is under
# prim:DualGroundingShape; an ungrounded class flips SP1's q_universality false").
#
# WHAT THIS FILE FULFILS (the committed T2–T10 contract). The plan Task T11 scope is "Every new crs:
# carrier/tower/geometer/plane/product owl:Class". This file brings EVERY such coordinate-chart OBJECT
# class UNDER the SP1 dual-grounding law — all 23 of them, not merely five — by giving each the SAME
# grounding cluster SP1's realization.ttl / taiji.ttl give each of the 59 tower classes. The full set:
#   CARRIERS (carriers.ttl T2):  crs:TaggedByteCarrier (B_rgb progenitor), crs:AtlasByteCarrier (Q_A),
#       crs:GraphByteCarrier (Q_G), crs:UntaggedBytePayload (shared untagged RGB x Vec(Oct) payload).
#   TOWERS (towers.ttl T3):      crs:UrnRoleTower (K_* progenitor), crs:SubjectTower (K_S),
#       crs:ObjectTower (K_O), crs:PredicateTower (K_P), crs:UrnTowerAxis (a URN-tower axis position).
#   GEOMETERS (geometers.ttl T5/T6):  crs:Geometer (progenitor), crs:RoleGeometer (rank-3 S-O-P),
#       crs:QuarkGridGeometer (rank-2 quark grid), crs:GeometerAxis (a geometer axis), crs:QuarkGrid
#       (the 3x3 grid).
#   PLANES (geometers.ttl T6, Q3):  crs:PlaneGeometer (progenitor), crs:HoneycombPlaneGeometer (x,y),
#       crs:GeographicPlaneGeometer (lon,lat), crs:RolePairProjectionPlane (sub-progenitor),
#       crs:SubjectObjectPlane, crs:SubjectPredicatePlane, crs:ObjectPredicatePlane (the symmetric family).
#   PRODUCT (geometers.ttl T7):  crs:CarrierProduct (K = K_A x K_G x K_S x K_O x K_P).
#   POINT (derivation.ttl T8):   crs:CoordinatePoint (the derived-not-stored coordinatised point).
# These are the crs formal OBJECTS. What is DELIBERATELY LEFT OUTSIDE prim:FormalType (so NOT grounded
# here) is exactly the non-object machinery SP1's own doctrine keeps out — YonedaShape's comment: "The
# arrow and presheaf classes ... are deliberately NOT rdfs:subClassOf* prim:FormalType": (a) the physical
# Frames / Kleisli arrows (crs:ForgetfulTagFrame, crs:LexToUrnBridge, crs:ColourOnlyProjection,
# crs:CoordinateDerivation, crs:ZDerivation, crs:OrderProjection — each rdfs:subClassOf prim:Realization,
# a bare owl:Class NOT under prim:FormalType, governed instead by prim:RealizationShape); (b) the arrows /
# projections of the product (crs:ProductArrow, crs:FactorComponentArrow, crs:FactorProjection and its
# children crs:CarrierTagProjection / crs:RoleTowerProjection); (c) the crs-minted SP4-seeding effect
# losses (crs:RoleDropEffect, crs:HashPrefixTruncation, crs:RoleOrderEffect — bare owl:Class, never a
# prim:frameEffect value, never under prim:FormalType); (d) the RGB colour channels (crs:ColourChannel /
# crs:RedChannel / crs:GreenChannel / crs:BlueChannel — SP1's prim:RGB code space RE-VIEWED, already
# floor-grounded via crs:groundsColourOctet -> prim:Red/Green/Blue, the T4 positional-collapse negative
# space, not a new SP3 formal chart object); (e) the provisional SP6 atlas-glossary forward reference
# (crs:AtlasGlossary, silm:isProvisional true — its grounding belongs to SP6, honestly deferred in v1).
# For each grounded object T11 reuses SP1's vocabulary WHOLESALE (prim:Realization / prim:PhysicalEncoding
# / prim:Primitive / prim:RepresentablePresheaf / prim:RhoComponent / prim:IdentityArrow /
# prim:RealizationTransport / prim:EncodingLoss / prim:presheafOlog), SELECT-not-mint (the SP2
# aob:groundingClaim discipline), never authoring a new prim:Effect member nor a new law. The five
# clusters authored first below (crs:CarrierProduct / crs:CoordinatePoint / crs:UrnTowerAxis /
# crs:GeometerAxis / crs:QuarkGrid) and the eighteen appended after them share one identical shape.
#
# THE PER-CLASS CLUSTER (identical shape for all 23 grounded objects, so the merged SP1 law stays green end to end):
#   (1) the pun + subtype edge :  <C> a prim:FormalType ; rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType
#         — <C> is ALREADY `a owl:Class` in its home file (carriers/towers/geometers/derivation.ttl); this file
#           adds ONLY the prim:FormalType pun + the subtype edge (so the per-file depth gate does not re-demand
#           the >=200-char class comment here — it lives with the class's original definition). Over the MERGED
#           graph <C> is then a genuine owl:Class + FormalType-tower class, so SP1's prim:DualGroundingShape AND
#           q_universality now TARGET it (the reused tooth) and its carrier's prim:interpretAs closes q_colimit_roundtrip.
#   (2) dual-grounding forward edges on <C> :  prim:realizesAs crs:realize_<C> ; prim:rhoObject crs:carrier_<C>
#   (3) the realization rho (Frame/Kleisli arrow) :  crs:realize_<C> a prim:Realization ; prim:realizesFrom <C> ;
#           prim:encoding + prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_<C> ; prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss
#         — satisfies prim:DualGroundingShape (the self arm) + prim:RealizationShape (frameOutput+frameEffect).
#   (4) the reflexive byte carrier :  crs:carrier_<C> a prim:PhysicalEncoding ; prim:bitWidth 8 ;
#           prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral ; prim:interpretAs <C>
#         — the octet-vector floor every crs carrier/tower descends into (design §2.2/§2.3: "descend from the
#           octet-vector floor"; bitWidth 8 / EndianNeutral is the SP2 prim:StringUtf8ByteVector idiom);
#           satisfies prim:EncodingShape (bitWidth 0..128, byteOrder in {LE,BE,EndianNeutral}, interpretAs ->
#           a FormalType) and closes q_colimit_reflexive (physicalFacet --interpretAs--> formalFacet).
#   (5) the glued taiji primitive :  crs:prim_<C> a prim:Primitive ; prim:formalFacet <C> ;
#           prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_<C> ; prim:gluedBy crs:realize_<C>
#         — the colimit object binding <C>'s yin to its yang by rho (q_colimit_reflexive / q_colimit_universal).
#   (6) the literal-Yoneda apparatus (keeps SP1's prim:YonedaShape green, since (1) also makes <C> a target of
#       it): crs:repr_<C> a prim:RepresentablePresheaf , prim:OlogObject ; prim:representableOf <C> ;
#           prim:yonedaPoint crs:id_<C> ; prim:homSetHasArrow crs:id_<C> ; prim:inPresheafOlog prim:presheafOlog ,
#       with <C> prim:yonedaObject crs:repr_<C> ; the reflexive Yoneda point crs:id_<C> a prim:IdentityArrow
#       (prim:arrowDom = prim:arrowCod = <C>) and its identity realization-transport crs:rt_id_<C> a
#       prim:RealizationTransport (prim:transportOf crs:id_<C>, prim:isTransportIdentity true, transportDom =
#       transportCod = crs:carrier_<C>) so SP1's q_functor_identity stays total; and the natural-transformation
#       component crs:rhoNat_<C> a prim:RhoComponent ; prim:rhoComponentAt <C> (prim:rhoComponentSource
#       crs:repr_<C>, prim:rhoComponentTarget crs:carrier_<C>) so YonedaShape's naturality clause holds.
#
# THE T11 TOOTH + PROBE (see crs.queries.sparql q_chart_dual_grounded). q_chart_dual_grounded REUSES SP1's
# q_universality logic scoped to crs: it is FALSE on the pre-T11 graph (no crs class was prim:FormalType) and
# TRUE here. Probe of record (reusing SP1 prim:DualGroundingShape's OrphanB teeth exactly): injecting
# `crs:probeOrphanChart a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType` (an ungrounded crs FormalType class)
# flips SP1 prim:DualGroundingShape conforms True->False over the merged graph, SP1 q_universality True->False,
# and q_chart_dual_grounded True->False; equivalently, STRIPPING crs:realize_CarrierProduct (its
# prim:realizesAs / prim:realizesFrom edges) leaves crs:CarrierProduct rdfs:subClassOf+ prim:FormalType with
# no grounding on its line and flips the same three — proving the grounding is load-bearing, not decorative.
#
# Corpus-agnostic v1 (Directive 13): zero corpus instances — pure grounding structure over the 23 coordinate-
# chart object classes. Author-scope: basicttl/crs/ only. Consumed by: SP1's re-run prim:DualGroundingShape / q_universality
# / q_colimit_* / q_yoneda_* / prim:YonedaShape / prim:EncodingShape over the merged graph.
# Design spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-08-w2-sp3-sop-tower-crs-law-design.md (§3, §4)
# Plan:        docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-09-w2-sp3-sop-tower-crs-law-plan.md (Task T11)
# =====================================================================================

@prefix crs:  <urn:silmaril:crs:#> .
@prefix prim: <urn:silmaril:prim:#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .


# =====================================================================================
# (1) crs:CarrierProduct — the five-factor Helios product K = K_A x K_G x K_S x K_O x K_P (the PRODUCT).
# =====================================================================================
crs:CarrierProduct a prim:FormalType ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType ;
    prim:realizesAs crs:realize_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:rhoObject  crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:yonedaObject crs:repr_CarrierProduct .

crs:carrier_CarrierProduct a prim:PhysicalEncoding ;
    prim:bitWidth 8 ;
    prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral ;
    prim:interpretAs crs:CarrierProduct ;
    rdfs:label "K carrier: five-factor product as an octet-vector layout" ;
    rdfs:comment "The reflexive byte carrier of the five-factor Helios product K = K_A x K_G x K_S x K_O x K_P: the octet-vector (Vec(Oct)) layout into which the flattened five-tuple of factor payloads serialises, prim:bitWidth 8 per octet occurrence, prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral (the byte-vector granule carries no multi-unit endianness), prim:interpretAs crs:CarrierProduct so the physical yang closes back onto its own formal yin (q_colimit_reflexive). It is the SP2 prim:StringUtf8ByteVector octet-vector idiom reused, not re-minted." .

crs:realize_CarrierProduct a prim:Realization ;
    prim:realizesFrom crs:CarrierProduct ;
    prim:encoding    crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss ;
    rdfs:label "rho: CarrierProduct |-> octet-vector layout (five-tuple flatten; EncodingLoss)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The dual-grounding realization rho of crs:CarrierProduct — a Frame / Kleisli arrow of the SP1 realization monad gluing the product object to its octet-vector carrier: prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_CarrierProduct (X, the physical byte layout) and prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss (Y, the honest loss of flattening the five-factor tuple into one linear octet stream — a SELECTED member of SP1's closed prim:Effect family, never a new effect). This is the self arm SP1's prim:DualGroundingShape reads (prim:realizesFrom crs:CarrierProduct), the reused SP1 tooth Task T11 owes the product class." .

crs:prim_CarrierProduct a prim:Primitive ;
    prim:formalFacet   crs:CarrierProduct ;
    prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:gluedBy       crs:realize_CarrierProduct ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive CarrierProduct (taiji: K (+) octet-vector layout)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The colimit-taiji primitive of crs:CarrierProduct — the glued object of the twin-olog diagram binding its formal yin (prim:formalFacet crs:CarrierProduct) to its physical yang (prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_CarrierProduct) by the realization rho (prim:gluedBy crs:realize_CarrierProduct). Its presence makes the product a genuine dual-grounded prim:Primitive over the merged floor, not a bare owl:Class, satisfying SP1's q_colimit_reflexive / q_colimit_universal." .

crs:repr_CarrierProduct a prim:RepresentablePresheaf , prim:OlogObject ;
    prim:representableOf crs:CarrierProduct ;
    prim:yonedaPoint     crs:id_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:homSetHasArrow  crs:id_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:inPresheafOlog  prim:presheafOlog ;
    rdfs:label "Hom(-, CarrierProduct)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The representable presheaf Hom(-, crs:CarrierProduct) = the image of the product object under the Yoneda embedding yo, carrying its Yoneda point prim:yonedaPoint crs:id_CarrierProduct (the identity element of Hom(K, K)). It puts crs:CarrierProduct in the object image of yo so SP1's prim:YonedaShape (which now targets it, since T11 makes it rdfs:subClassOf* prim:FormalType) stays green." .

crs:id_CarrierProduct a prim:IdentityArrow ;
    prim:arrowDom crs:CarrierProduct ;
    prim:arrowCod crs:CarrierProduct ;
    rdfs:label "id_CarrierProduct" ;
    rdfs:comment "The identity morphism id at crs:CarrierProduct (prim:arrowDom = prim:arrowCod = crs:CarrierProduct), the unit of arrow composition at the product object and the reflexive Yoneda point of Hom(-, crs:CarrierProduct). Its presence keeps SP1's thin formal category total over the new object." .

crs:rt_id_CarrierProduct a prim:RealizationTransport ;
    prim:transportOf crs:id_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:transportDom crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:transportCod crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:isTransportIdentity true ;
    rdfs:label "rho(id_CarrierProduct) = id on the K octet-vector carrier" ;
    rdfs:comment "The realization functor rho applied to id_CarrierProduct: the identity RealizationTransport at rho(CarrierProduct) = crs:carrier_CarrierProduct (prim:transportDom = prim:transportCod = crs:carrier_CarrierProduct, prim:isTransportIdentity true), so rho preserves identities at the new object and SP1's q_functor_identity stays total over the merged graph." .

crs:rhoNat_CarrierProduct a prim:RhoComponent ;
    prim:rhoComponentAt     crs:CarrierProduct ;
    prim:rhoComponentSource crs:repr_CarrierProduct ;
    prim:rhoComponentTarget crs:carrier_CarrierProduct ;
    rdfs:label "rho component at CarrierProduct: yo(K) -> rho(K)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The component at crs:CarrierProduct of the natural transformation rho: yo => R (prim:rhoComponentSource crs:repr_CarrierProduct = yo(K), prim:rhoComponentTarget crs:carrier_CarrierProduct = rho(K)). Its presence at the object is the prerequisite for naturality, so SP1's prim:YonedaShape naturality clause and q_naturality_commutes stay green with the product added." .


# =====================================================================================
# (2) crs:CoordinatePoint — the coordinatised point (coordinates DERIVED, never stored) (the POINT).
# =====================================================================================
crs:CoordinatePoint a prim:FormalType ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType ;
    prim:realizesAs crs:realize_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:rhoObject  crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:yonedaObject crs:repr_CoordinatePoint .

crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint a prim:PhysicalEncoding ;
    prim:bitWidth 8 ;
    prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral ;
    prim:interpretAs crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    rdfs:label "point carrier: coordinate tuple as an octet-vector" ;
    rdfs:comment "The reflexive byte carrier of a crs:CoordinatePoint: the octet-vector serialisation of the point's derived coordinate tuple, prim:bitWidth 8 per octet occurrence, prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral, prim:interpretAs crs:CoordinatePoint (physical yang closes onto formal yin). The coordinates themselves remain DERIVED (each a crs:CoordinateDerivation frameOutput, T8); this carrier is only the byte floor the point's identity descends into, reusing the SP1 octet-vector idiom." .

crs:realize_CoordinatePoint a prim:Realization ;
    prim:realizesFrom crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:encoding    crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss ;
    rdfs:label "rho: CoordinatePoint |-> octet-vector carrier (EncodingLoss)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The dual-grounding realization rho of crs:CoordinatePoint — the Frame gluing the point object to its octet-vector carrier: prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint and prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss (the SELECTED SP1 closed-family loss of serialising the point identity to bytes). It is the self arm prim:DualGroundingShape reads (prim:realizesFrom crs:CoordinatePoint), the reused SP1 grounding T11 owes the point class per its comment 'T11 adds the reused dual-grounding'." .

crs:prim_CoordinatePoint a prim:Primitive ;
    prim:formalFacet   crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:gluedBy       crs:realize_CoordinatePoint ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive CoordinatePoint (taiji: point (+) octet-vector carrier)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The colimit-taiji primitive of crs:CoordinatePoint binding its formal yin (prim:formalFacet crs:CoordinatePoint) to its physical yang (prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint) by rho (prim:gluedBy crs:realize_CoordinatePoint), making the coordinatised point a dual-grounded prim:Primitive over the merged floor (q_colimit_reflexive / q_colimit_universal)." .

crs:repr_CoordinatePoint a prim:RepresentablePresheaf , prim:OlogObject ;
    prim:representableOf crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:yonedaPoint     crs:id_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:homSetHasArrow  crs:id_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:inPresheafOlog  prim:presheafOlog ;
    rdfs:label "Hom(-, CoordinatePoint)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The representable presheaf Hom(-, crs:CoordinatePoint), the image of the point object under the Yoneda embedding yo, carrying its Yoneda point prim:yonedaPoint crs:id_CoordinatePoint. It keeps crs:CoordinatePoint in the object image of yo so SP1's prim:YonedaShape stays green with the point brought under prim:FormalType by T11." .

crs:id_CoordinatePoint a prim:IdentityArrow ;
    prim:arrowDom crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:arrowCod crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    rdfs:label "id_CoordinatePoint" ;
    rdfs:comment "The identity morphism id at crs:CoordinatePoint (prim:arrowDom = prim:arrowCod = crs:CoordinatePoint), the unit of composition at the point object and the reflexive Yoneda point of Hom(-, crs:CoordinatePoint), keeping the thin formal category total over the new object." .

crs:rt_id_CoordinatePoint a prim:RealizationTransport ;
    prim:transportOf crs:id_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:transportDom crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:transportCod crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:isTransportIdentity true ;
    rdfs:label "rho(id_CoordinatePoint) = id on the point octet-vector carrier" ;
    rdfs:comment "rho applied to id_CoordinatePoint: the identity RealizationTransport at rho(CoordinatePoint) = crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint (transportDom = transportCod = crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint, prim:isTransportIdentity true), so rho preserves identities and SP1's q_functor_identity stays total." .

crs:rhoNat_CoordinatePoint a prim:RhoComponent ;
    prim:rhoComponentAt     crs:CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:rhoComponentSource crs:repr_CoordinatePoint ;
    prim:rhoComponentTarget crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint ;
    rdfs:label "rho component at CoordinatePoint" ;
    rdfs:comment "The component at crs:CoordinatePoint of rho: yo => R (source crs:repr_CoordinatePoint = yo(point), target crs:carrier_CoordinatePoint = rho(point)), the naturality prerequisite that keeps SP1's prim:YonedaShape naturality clause and q_naturality_commutes green." .


# =====================================================================================
# (3) crs:UrnTowerAxis — a role-tower axis position (the per-index prim:URN coordinate) (the TOWER axis).
# =====================================================================================
crs:UrnTowerAxis a prim:FormalType ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType ;
    prim:realizesAs crs:realize_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:rhoObject  crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:yonedaObject crs:repr_UrnTowerAxis .

crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis a prim:PhysicalEncoding ;
    prim:bitWidth 8 ;
    prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral ;
    prim:interpretAs crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    rdfs:label "tower-axis carrier: URN as a UTF-8 octet stream" ;
    rdfs:comment "The reflexive byte carrier of a crs:UrnTowerAxis: the UTF-8 octet stream a prim:URN tower term reads as (the byte floor of the Identifier tower), prim:bitWidth 8 per octet occurrence, prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral, prim:interpretAs crs:UrnTowerAxis. A tower axis value is a URN-tower term (never a scalar, per T3 crs:AxisUrnTowerShape); this carrier is its octet-vector descent, the same UTF-8 idiom SP2 uses for aob:sourceNodeUrn." .

crs:realize_UrnTowerAxis a prim:Realization ;
    prim:realizesFrom crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:encoding    crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss ;
    rdfs:label "rho: UrnTowerAxis |-> URN UTF-8 octet stream (EncodingLoss)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The dual-grounding realization rho of crs:UrnTowerAxis — the Frame gluing the tower-axis object to its UTF-8 octet carrier: prim:frameOutput crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis and prim:frameEffect prim:EncodingLoss (the SELECTED SP1 closed-family Unicode-normalisation/UTF-8 loss). It is the self arm prim:DualGroundingShape reads (prim:realizesFrom crs:UrnTowerAxis) — the reused dual-grounding of the tower classes T11 owes per crs:UrnTowerAxis's comment." .

crs:prim_UrnTowerAxis a prim:Primitive ;
    prim:formalFacet   crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:gluedBy       crs:realize_UrnTowerAxis ;
    rdfs:label "Primitive UrnTowerAxis (taiji: URN axis (+) UTF-8 octets)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The colimit-taiji primitive of crs:UrnTowerAxis binding its formal yin (prim:formalFacet crs:UrnTowerAxis) to its physical yang (prim:physicalFacet crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis) by rho (prim:gluedBy crs:realize_UrnTowerAxis), making the URN tower axis a dual-grounded prim:Primitive over the merged floor (q_colimit_reflexive / q_colimit_universal)." .

crs:repr_UrnTowerAxis a prim:RepresentablePresheaf , prim:OlogObject ;
    prim:representableOf crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:yonedaPoint     crs:id_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:homSetHasArrow  crs:id_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:inPresheafOlog  prim:presheafOlog ;
    rdfs:label "Hom(-, UrnTowerAxis)" ;
    rdfs:comment "The representable presheaf Hom(-, crs:UrnTowerAxis), the image of the tower-axis object under the Yoneda embedding yo, carrying its Yoneda point prim:yonedaPoint crs:id_UrnTowerAxis, keeping the axis in the object image of yo so SP1's prim:YonedaShape stays green under T11's prim:FormalType wiring." .

crs:id_UrnTowerAxis a prim:IdentityArrow ;
    prim:arrowDom crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:arrowCod crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    rdfs:label "id_UrnTowerAxis" ;
    rdfs:comment "The identity morphism id at crs:UrnTowerAxis (prim:arrowDom = prim:arrowCod = crs:UrnTowerAxis), the unit of composition at the tower-axis object and the reflexive Yoneda point of Hom(-, crs:UrnTowerAxis), keeping the thin formal category total over the new object." .

crs:rt_id_UrnTowerAxis a prim:RealizationTransport ;
    prim:transportOf crs:id_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:transportDom crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:transportCod crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:isTransportIdentity true ;
    rdfs:label "rho(id_UrnTowerAxis) = id on the URN octet carrier" ;
    rdfs:comment "rho applied to id_UrnTowerAxis: the identity RealizationTransport at rho(UrnTowerAxis) = crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis (transportDom = transportCod = crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis, prim:isTransportIdentity true), so rho preserves identities and SP1's q_functor_identity stays total." .

crs:rhoNat_UrnTowerAxis a prim:RhoComponent ;
    prim:rhoComponentAt     crs:UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:rhoComponentSource crs:repr_UrnTowerAxis ;
    prim:rhoComponentTarget crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis ;
    rdfs:label "rho component at UrnTowerAxis" ;
    rdfs:comment "The component at crs:UrnTowerAxis of rho: yo => R (source crs:repr_UrnTowerAxis = yo(axis), target crs:carrier_UrnTowerAxis = rho(axis)), the naturality prerequisite keeping SP1's prim:YonedaShape naturality clause and q_naturality_commutes green." .


# =====================================================================================
# (4) crs:GeometerAxis — a per-geometer axis, one coordinate dimension of a geometer (the GEOMETER axis).
# =====================================================================================
crs:GeometerAxis a prim:FormalType ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prim:FormalType ;
    prim:realizesAs crs:realize_GeometerAxis ;
    prim:rhoObject  crs:carrier_GeometerAxis ;
    prim:yonedaObject crs:repr_GeometerAxis .

crs:carrier_GeometerAxis a prim:PhysicalEncoding ;
    prim:bitWidth 8 ;
    prim:byteOrder prim:EndianNeutral ;
    prim:interpretAs crs:GeometerAxis ;
    rdfs:label "geometer-axis carrier: coordinate value as an octet-vector" ;
