    rdfs:comment "The materialised ancestral grounding path witnessing that crs:GraphByteCarrier is ALSO grounded through its realized proper ancestor crs:TaggedByteCarrier (crs:GraphByteCarrier rdfs:subClassOf+ crs:TaggedByteCarrier, both dual-grounded FormalType objects over the merged graph). crs:GraphByteCarrier keeps its OWN direct grounding (its own reflexive carrier + prim:Realization + prim:Primitive) UNCHANGED; this ADDS the transported second grounding: prim:ancestralViaTransport crs:rt_sub_GraphByteCarrier_TaggedByteCarrier is the rho-image of the taxonomic subtyping, and prim:ancestralLandsIn crs:carrier_TaggedByteCarrier = rho(crs:TaggedByteCarrier) is the ancestor's own realization carrier the transport's prim:transportCod resolves to exactly. SP1's q_ancestral_transport_resolves reads this pair as covered." .

